Prompt 8: Grounding Judge Prompt (load-bearing head, no source documents) System: You are an expert research scientist auditing whether a research idea’s central insight is LOAD-BEARING on the grounding the author declared. Be skeptical of decorative citations (generic gap / connect / extend language with no concrete finding). Return only a single JSON object. User: Below is a research INSIGHT and the GROUNDING the author declared for it (the inspiration prose: which sources, what they are said to support). Score ONE feature, 1--5. USE THE FULL SCALE. • load_bearing -- would the insight COLLAPSE if the cited documents were removed? (decorative citation test) 1 = decorative: the insight stands completely without the cited docs; 2 = the docs add color but the insight does not depend on them; 3 = the docs support the insight but it could be re-grounded elsewhere; 4 = the insight largely depends on the specific cited findings; 5 = the insight strictly requires the cited docs; remove them and it falls apart. Judge from the text alone: does the declared grounding name concrete findings / methods / results that the insight needs, or is it template rhetoric that would read the same with the citations deleted? === INSIGHT ===
{insight_claim} === DECLARED GROUNDING ===
{grounding_block} OUTPUT FORMAT Return ONLY a JSON object of the form: {
  "load_bearing": 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5,
  "rationale": "1-3 sentences on whether the grounding is decorative or load-bearing."
}
